---
description: Conventional Commits 1.0.0 for planning, PRs, and commit messages
alwaysApply: true
---

When planning work, writing PR descriptions, or drafting/reviewing commit messages, follow Conventional Commits 1.0.0.

```
<type>[optional scope][optional !]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- `feat` / `fix` are required types for features and bug fixes; other types MAY be used (`docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`).
- Breaking changes use `!` before `:` and/or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
- Adopt going forward; do not rewrite published history.

Full specification (MUST/SHOULD rules, examples, FAQ): `.agents/skills/agent-review/commit-message/SKILL.md`.
